1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,135
The evidence meeting was held in a shop that had been converted into an office.

2
00:00:04,135 --> 00:00:11,855
A wooden counter, a traditional sign, and a book of invoices remained from the previous owner.

3
00:00:11,855 --> 00:00:16,269
“We need to establish what we owe,” the woman said.

4
00:00:16,269 --> 00:00:28,313
“The cost of the film is not the cost of the work.” One part of the room was still a shopping aisle, and his face when he saw it was worth the trip.

5
00:00:28,313 --> 00:00:36,847
Their pay came from a corporation with an outstanding tax case and a pension fund that it had quietly replaced with a loan.

6
00:00:36,847 --> 00:00:44,586
An investor and a banker came to the exhibition; a lobbyist came too, and stayed for the wine.

7
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:48,880
“The consumer pays twice,” the dealer said.

8
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:59,744
“Once in cash, once in attention.” Since the contract began, no one had written that sentence down until now.

9
00:00:59,744 --> 00:01:04,269
The arrival of the supply figures changed the argument.

10
00:01:04,269 --> 00:01:20,811
A supplier of advertising space, a musician who wrote derivative jingles, and a young capitalist from the party of the premier all agreed on one point: the demand for goods was a threat to the small shop, not a help.

11
00:01:20,811 --> 00:01:27,626
They could read the writing on the wall, and they could not write it off as pessimism.

12
00:01:27,626 --> 00:01:35,700
The team published a one-page report, with a workshop and an open workout for anyone who wanted to read it.

13
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:43,769
Participation was voluntary, the initiation was a cup of tea, and the overtime was unpaid.

14
00:01:43,769 --> 00:01:47,813
“That is the compensation,” Maya said.

15
00:01:47,813 --> 00:02:00,592
“The mutual appreciation of people who cannot afford to leave.” Together they checked every figure twice; whether the client would accept it remained a question.

16
00:02:00,592 --> 00:02:08,641
Their earnings were smaller than the assistance they had received, and the second part of the study was harder to write.

17
00:02:08,641 --> 00:02:15,745
Some of them would fulfil the contract; some would convey the problem to the council instead.

18
00:02:15,745 --> 00:02:23,019
It was a valuable lesson and an earnest one, and the shopping street outside told the same story.

19
00:02:23,019 --> 00:02:32,113
The income was small and the room was big; a copy of the contract was available in the corridor, and nobody had read it.

20
00:02:32,113 --> 00:02:50,871
“When the consumer is also the servant,” Lin wrote, “the exhibition is the only honest form of advertising.” They would continue, but they could not remain silent, and the difference between those two verbs was the whole fourth arc.
